# Double-width and double-height lines: DECSWL, DECDWL and DECDHL (`ESC # 5`, `# 6`, `# 3`, `# 4`).
#
# The size belongs to a row and moves with it. On a double-width or double-height row every
# character is two columns wide, so only the first half of the columns can be reached: the screens
# here are 10 columns wide and a sized row has 5. `line-size` reads the row's size; the text checks
# show every cell of the row, the hidden half included.

test DECDWL makes the cursor's row double-width
spec xterm ctlseqs: ESC # 6 DEC double-width line (DECDWL); VT510 DECDWL
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#6
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 double-width
line-size 3 single
line-size 4 single

test DECDHL sets the top half and the bottom half
spec xterm ctlseqs: ESC # 3 DEC double-height line, top half (DECDHL); ESC # 4 bottom half; VT510 DECDHL
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#3\e[3;1H\e#4
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 double-height-top
line-size 3 double-height-bottom
line-size 4 single

test DECSWL makes the row single again
spec xterm ctlseqs: ESC # 5 DEC single-width line (DECSWL); VT510 DECSWL
size 10 2
feed \e#6\e#3\e#5
line-size 1 single

test the last size set on a row is the one it has
spec VT510 DECDWL and DECDHL: the attribute is the line's
size 10 2
feed \e#3\e#6
line-size 1 double-width

test the cursor cannot go past half the columns on a double-width row
spec VT510 DECDWL: a double-width line holds half as many characters (40 in 80 columns)
size 10 3
feed \e#6\e[1;9H
cursor 1,5

test cursor forward stops at half the columns
spec VT510 DECDWL, CUF: the cursor stops at the right margin, which is half the columns on such a line
size 10 3
feed \e#6\e[100C
cursor 1,5

test a double-height row holds half the columns too
spec VT510 DECDHL: the two halves are double-width lines
size 10 3
feed \e[2;1H\e#3\e[100C
cursor 2,5

test a row not sized keeps all columns
spec VT510 DECSWL: single-width lines hold the whole width
size 10 3
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[1;1H\e[100C
cursor 1,10

test the cursor moved to a double-width row is brought inside it
convention the cursor cannot be where a double-width row has no column, so a vertical move onto such a row keeps the nearest one
size 10 3
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[1;9H\e[B
cursor 2,5

test setting the size moves a cursor that is past the new half
convention the cursor cannot be where the row has no column
size 10 3
feed abcdefgh\e#6
cursor 1,5

test text wraps at half the columns of a double-width row
spec VT510 DECDWL and DECAWM: the line wraps at its right margin, the half of the columns
size 10 4
feed \e#6abcdefg
screen
|abcde|
|fg|
cursor 2,3
wrapped 1 no

test with autowrap off the last visible column is overwritten
spec VT510 DECAWM reset: characters past the right margin overwrite the last column; on a double-width line it is the half
size 10 3
feed \e[?7l\e#6abcdefgh
screen
|abcdh|
cursor 1,5

test a wide character that does not fit the half wraps whole
spec VT510 DECAWM: a character that does not fit goes to the next line
size 8 3
feed \e#6abc\u{4e16}
screen
|abc|
|\u{4e16}|
cursor 2,3

test a tab stops at the last visible column
spec VT510 HT: the cursor stops at the right margin without a stop
size 20 3
feed \e#6\t\t\t
cursor 1,10

test the cells past half are kept, hidden, when the size is set
convention the VT510 manual does not say what becomes of characters beyond the half; they stay in the row, hidden, and DECSWL shows them again
size 10 3
feed abcdefghij\e[1;1H\e#6
screen
|abcdefghij|
line-size 1 double-width
cursor 1,1
feed \e#5
screen
|abcdefghij|
line-size 1 single

test a double-width line does not change what is written on a single one
spec VT510 DECSWL: single-width lines are unchanged
size 10 3
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[1;1Habcdefghij
screen
|abcdefghij|
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 double-width

test a size moves with its row when the region scrolls down
spec VT510 DECDWL: the attribute is part of the line; RI scrolls lines down
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[1;1H\eM
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 single
line-size 3 double-width
line-size 4 single

test a size moves with its row when the screen scrolls up
spec VT510 DECDWL: the attribute is part of the line; IND scrolls lines up
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[3;1H\e#4\e[4;1H\n
line-size 1 double-width
line-size 2 double-height-bottom
line-size 3 single
line-size 4 single

test a line that enters by scrolling is single
spec VT510 DECDWL: new lines are single-width
size 10 3
feed \e#6\e[3;1H\n\n
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 single
line-size 3 single

test a size moves with its row when lines are inserted
spec VT510 IL: the lines move down with their attributes; the new line is a normal one
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e[L
line-size 2 single
line-size 3 double-width
line-size 4 single

test a size moves with its row when lines are deleted
spec VT510 DL: the lines move up with their attributes
size 10 4
feed \e[3;1H\e#3\e[2;1H\e[M
line-size 2 double-height-top
line-size 3 single

test a size stays with the lines of a scrolling region
spec VT510 DECSTBM and DECDWL: a scroll inside the margins moves the lines with their attributes
size 10 5
feed \e[3;1H\e#6\e[2;4r\e[4;1H\n
line-size 2 double-width
line-size 3 single
line-size 4 single
line-size 5 single

test a row outside a scrolling region keeps its size
spec VT510 DECSTBM: lines outside the margins do not scroll
size 10 5
feed \e[1;1H\e#6\e[2;4r\e[4;1H\n
line-size 1 double-width

test erasing in a line leaves its size
spec VT510 EL: erases characters; the attribute is the line's
size 10 3
feed \e#6abc\e[2K
screen
line-size 1 double-width

test erasing characters leaves the size
spec VT510 ECH: erases characters; the attribute is the line's
size 10 3
feed \e#6abc\e[1;1H\e[2X
screen
|  c|
line-size 1 double-width

test erase in display from the cursor resets the rows below, not the cursor's
convention ED blanks whole rows below the cursor, which lose their size; the cursor's row is only erased from the cursor
size 10 4
feed \e[1;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e#6\e[3;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e[J
line-size 1 double-width
line-size 2 double-width
line-size 3 single

test erase in display to the cursor resets the rows above, not the cursor's
convention ED blanks whole rows above the cursor, which lose their size; the cursor's row is only erased up to the cursor
size 10 4
feed \e[1;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e#6\e[3;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e[1J
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 double-width
line-size 3 double-width

test erase in display of everything resets every row
spec VT510 ED 2: erases the whole display; the lines become normal
size 10 4
feed \e[1;1H\e#6\e[2;1H\e#3\e[3;1H\e#4\e[2J
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 single
line-size 3 single
line-size 4 single

test the screen alignment test makes every row single
spec VT510 DECALN: fills the screen with E; every line is a single-width line
size 10 3
feed \e#6\e[2;1H\e#3\e#8
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 single

test a full reset makes every row single
spec VT510 RIS: returns the terminal to its initial state
size 10 3
feed \e#6\e[2;1H\e#3\ec
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 single

test insert characters works inside the half
spec VT510 ICH: characters move right up to the right margin, which is half the columns on such a line
size 10 3
feed abcdefghij\e[1;1H\e#6\e[2@
screen
|  abcfghij|

test delete characters works inside the half
spec VT510 DCH: characters move left, blanks enter at the right margin, which is half the columns on such a line
size 10 3
feed abcdefghij\e[1;1H\e#6\e[2P
screen
|cde  fghij|

test a resize keeps a double-width row as it is and never rewraps it
convention a double-width row keeps its cells and is not reflowed; the soft-wrapped lines around it are rewrapped as usual
size 10 3
feed abcdefghijklmno\e[1;1H\e#6\e[3;1H
resize 20 3
screen
|abcdefghij|
|klmno|
line-size 1 double-width
wrapped 1 no

test a resize crops a double-width row to the new width
convention a double-width row is cropped like the alternate screen's rows
size 10 3
feed abcdefghij\e[1;1H\e#6
resize 6 3
screen
|abcdef|
line-size 1 double-width

test a resize keeps the size of the rows around it
convention the other rows are reflowed as before and keep their sizes
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1H\e#3\e[3;1H\e#4
resize 14 4
line-size 1 single
line-size 2 double-height-top
line-size 3 double-height-bottom
line-size 4 single

test a double-height line is written on two rows with the same text
spec VT510 DECDHL: the same characters are written on both lines, top half and bottom half
size 10 3
feed \e#3Hello\r\n\e#4Hello
screen
|Hello|
|Hello|
line-size 1 double-height-top
line-size 2 double-height-bottom
cursor 2,5
